  "Question": "When the distance from the center of a circle to a line is greater than the radius, what is the relationship between the line and the circle?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "They intersect at 2 points",
    "B": "They are tangent",
    "C": "The line passes through the center",
    "D": "They are disjoint"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "When \\(d>r\\), there are no common points. This is called being disjoint.",
